        <h1 itemprop="headline">Why calendar weeks beat rolling 7-day averages</h1>
        <p itemprop="description">A rolling 7-day average never finishes: the window moves every morning, so yesterday's answer keeps getting rewritten. A calendar week ends, stays ended, and can be compared. That is the argument for building WeekScale this way.</p>
